per view. Not 10% more, not double, 160

00:09:16.480 --> 00:09:20.440
times more. So, that's not luck, that is

00:09:18.480 --> 00:09:22.040
targeting the right audience with the

00:09:20.440 --> 00:09:23.880
right offer and measuring the right

00:09:22.040 --> 00:09:25.720
thing. So, stop watching the scorecard

00:09:23.880 --> 00:09:27.160
that nobody pays you for. Oh, and by the

00:09:25.720 --> 00:09:28.320
way, my other channels can do even more

00:09:27.160 --> 00:09:29.760
than that. So, my niche channel, for

00:09:28.320 --> 00:09:31.080
instance, which is all about YouTube for

00:09:29.760 --> 00:09:32.680
business owners and goes over

00:09:31.080 --> 00:09:35.560
higher-level stuff, that channel makes

00:09:32.680 --> 00:09:37.920
over $4,000 per 1,000 views. So, it's

00:09:35.560 --> 00:09:39.160
making over 1,000 times more per view

00:09:37.920 --> 00:09:41.440
than the average YouTube channel. And

00:09:39.160 --> 00:09:43.520
look, everything we talked about so far,

00:09:41.440 --> 00:09:45.800
niche, compounding, foot traffic,

00:09:43.520 --> 00:09:48.040
consistency, the right stat to actually

00:09:45.800 --> 00:09:50.120
pay attention to, none of it matters if

00:09:48.040 --> 00:09:51.840
you don't have this last piece, which is

00:09:50.120 --> 00:09:54.040
the offer, right? And I've seen creators

00:09:51.840 --> 00:09:55.920
get their first video to 500,000 views,

00:09:54.040 --> 00:09:57.800
half a million people watching, and they

00:09:55.920 --> 00:10:00.840
made almost nothing from it because they

00:09:57.800 --> 00:10:03.360
had no call to action, no email list,

00:10:00.840 --> 00:10:04.600
and no offer. No place to send all of

00:10:03.360 --> 00:10:06.640
those people. And by the way, I'm not

00:10:04.600 --> 00:10:09.440
making this up. This is a real client.

00:10:06.640 --> 00:10:11.200
500,000 views just evaporated. So, that

00:10:09.440 --> 00:10:13.160
is what I call the offer gap. You can do

00:10:11.200 --> 00:10:15.280
everything right on the content side and

00:10:13.160 --> 00:10:17.400
leave 90% of the money on the table

00:10:15.280 --> 00:10:18.920
because you forgot to build the bridge.

00:10:17.400 --> 00:10:20.720
And my client Joaquin is the perfect

00:10:18.920 --> 00:10:22.760
example of what happens when you close

00:10:20.720 --> 00:10:24.480
that gap. When I first met Joaquin, he

00:10:22.760 --> 00:10:25.840
was 18 years old with a small YouTube

00:10:24.480 --> 00:10:27.720
channel talking about engineering

00:10:25.840 --> 00:10:29.480
concepts and study tips. And he was a

00:10:27.720 --> 00:10:31.360
smart kid, decent content as well, but

00:10:29.480 --> 00:10:32.880
he wasn't making any money. And I've

00:10:31.360 --> 00:10:35.360
seen this exact pattern hundreds of

00:10:32.880 --> 00:10:37.000
times. The niche was too broad, and

00:10:35.360 --> 00:10:38.640
there was no clear path from I watched

00:10:37.000 --> 00:10:40.520
your video to I'm going to pay you to

00:10:38.640 --> 00:10:42.400
solve my problem. So, we completely

00:10:40.520 --> 00:10:44.280
pivoted his niche. Now, Joaquin is an

00:10:42.400 --> 00:10:45.880
international student who got into an

00:10:44.280 --> 00:10:47.680
elite Ivy League university,

00:10:45.880 --> 00:10:48.920
specifically UPenn at Wharton, which is

00:10:47.680 --> 00:10:50.880
one of the best business schools in the

00:10:48.920 --> 00:10:53.040
world. And we built his entire channel

00:10:50.880 --> 00:10:55.040
around that unfair advantage, helping

00:10:53.040 --> 00:10:56.920
international students get into Ivy

00:10:55.040 --> 00:10:59.680
League schools, or at the very least

00:10:56.920 --> 00:11:01.560
elite universities. So, new niche, clear

00:10:59.680 --> 00:11:03.040
offer, and clear audience. And within a

00:11:01.560 --> 00:11:05.880
short period of time, Joaquin went from

00:11:03.040 --> 00:11:08.200
making basically nothing to 80 5,000

00:11:05.880 --> 00:11:11.160
dollars in a single month as a teenager.

00:11:08.200 --> 00:11:13.000
So, same kid, same work ethic, different

00:11:11.160 --> 00:11:14.760
niche, and a clear offer at the end of

00:11:13.000 --> 00:11:17.040
every video. The content gets people in

00:11:14.760 --> 00:11:19.200
the door, the offer is how you get paid.

00:11:17.040 --> 00:11:21.200
Here's the thing, after coaching 500

00:11:19.200 --> 00:11:23.240
channels, it is never about working

00:11:21.200 --> 00:11:25.400
harder. It's about these fundamentals.

00:11:23.240 --> 00:11:27.400
Target people that are in pain, not the

00:11:25.400 --> 00:11:29.480
whitening crowd, be the only brain

00:11:27.400 --> 00:11:31.680
surgeon in the city, let the right early

00:11:29.480 --> 00:11:33.480
decisions compound, set up your hot dog

00:11:31.680 --> 00:11:35.200
stand where the crowd already is, show

00:11:33.480 --> 00:11:37.560
up every single day, track the one

00:11:35.200 --> 00:11:40.040
number that actually pays you, and close

00:11:37.560 --> 00:11:42.160
the offer gap. Because 500,000 views

00:11:40.040 --> 00:11:44.800
means nothing without somewhere to send

00:11:42.160 --> 00:11:47.160
people. So, pain point, niche, compound,

00:11:44.800 --> 00:11:49.840
foot traffic, show up, one stat, and the

00:11:47.160 --> 00:11:51.160
offer. That is the whole playbook. Now,

00:11:49.840 --> 00:11:53.200
you might be thinking, "This sounds

